// forbidden-tools-guard.bml — the PreToolUse door: a Bash call that runs sed, awk, perl or python is refused at the door.
//
//   <hook JSON on stdin> | ./fkwu observe/forbidden-tools-guard.bml
//
// stdin is the hook's JSON ({"tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"..."},...}). When the command runs a forbidden
// tool, stdout is one line, exactly
//   {"hookSpecificOutput":{"hookEventName":"PreToolUse","permissionDecision":"deny","permissionDecisionReason":"<what ran and what to use>"}}
// and the exit is 0. Otherwise nothing is printed (stdout is closed before fkwu's own answer line, so no byte arrives)
// and the exit is 0. A reading that did not arrive (empty or garbled stdin, no command field, another tool) prints nothing:
// the guard fails open. The reading is form-stdlib/bml/forbidden-tools-guard.bml over form-stdlib/bml/command-words.bml,
// which says what a command string can show and what it cannot (a variable that holds the tool, a script file that runs
// it, an alias). Registered for every Bash call by .claude/settings.json; delete that entry to switch it off.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/bml/stdin-source.bml form-stdlib/bml/forbidden-tools-guard.bml
section [form.bml] {
 hkg-answer(stdin-text());
}
